   "evidence": "`upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Units/Defs.lean:231-235` defines `npow := fun n a \u21a6 {val := a ^ n, inv := a\u207b\u00b9 ^ n}`; `val_pow_eq_pow_val ... := rfl` (Defs.lean:270) and `IsUnit.unit_spec ... := rfl` (Defs.lean:503). `Units.eq_inv_mul_iff_mul_eq` states `a = \u2191b\u207b\u00b9 * c \u2194 \u2191b * a = c` (Units/Basic.lean:76), i.e. the `\u2191(u ^ n)\u207b\u00b9` form, not the `(\u2191u\u207b\u00b9) ^ n` form written in the goals.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/Evolution/BetaFunction.lean",
   "fix": "Introduce one reusable helper, e.g. `lemma eq_inv_pow_mul {u : R\u02e3} {n : \u2115} {a b : R} (h : (u : R) ^ n * a = b) : a = (\u2191u\u207b\u00b9 : R) ^ n * b`, proved explicitly via `Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val`/`Units.val_inv_eq_inv_val`/`inv_pow`, and apply it (with `coe_linearCoeff`) at lines 228, 235, 242, 349. That removes the silent defeq without reinstating the four copies of coercion bookkeeping.",
   "issue": "`(Units.eq_inv_mul_iff_mul_eq (SubstGroup.linearCoeff F ^ 2)).mpr h` produces `a = \u2191(u ^ 2)\u207b\u00b9 * c`, but the stated goal is `(\u2191u\u207b\u00b9 : R) ^ 2 * ...`, and `h` is phrased in `coeff 1 F.toPowerSeries`, not `\u2191(linearCoeff F)`. It elaborates only because `\u2191(u ^ n)\u207b\u00b9` is syntactically `(\u2191u\u207b\u00b9) ^ n` after unfolding the `npow` field of `Units.instMonoid`, and `\u2191(IsUnit.unit h)` is `rfl`-equal to `coeff 1 F.toPowerSeries`. Nothing in the file says so; a change to that instance field breaks these statements with an opaque unification error. Same reliance at lines 228 (`unit_spec` only), 242 and 349.",
   "line": 235
  }
 ],
